# Death-penalty experience recovery through the 1.2 priest prayer (skill 17063).
#
# The victim (GM) reaches level 21 and adds 5 000 exp, so the next death loses the 5 % of the
# level span into `recoverable_exp` (80 % recoverable). The caster (GM) kills it at the Nui
# temple priest 502 spawn (`npc_spawns.json` UnitId 502 at 23039.76 11540.64 252.7, where both
# bots teleport). The victim revives with `/revive` (the GM revive keeps the recoverable exp)
# and casts 17063 the way the 1.2 priest window does (`X2Priest:RecoverExp` -> `CSStartSkill`,
# unit caster, the priest as target; the skill resolves its self target back to the caster and
# the effect needs a priest within 10 m). The recovery must answer with
# `SCRecoverableExpPacket` (zero left), `SCCharacterLaborPowerChangedPacket` (level 21 labor)
# and `SCExpChangedPacket`; the pre-#21 `NO_PERM` refusal would leave the exp lost.
#
# `castraw` is used instead of `cast` because `cast` drains for up to 8 s and would swallow the
# 6.5 s prayer's effect packets, which are what this suite asserts. It walks to the priest first,
# as the real client does; the prayer's 10 m priest check needs that.

suite exp-recovery
bot victim gm
bot caster gm

[caster]
gm level 21
# Both bots meet at the Nui temple priest 502 spawn (`npc_spawns.json` UnitId 502 at
# 23039.76 11540.64 252.7); the characters remember their last position between runs.
tp 23039.76 11540.64 252.7
pump 3
waitpeer 120 ${victim}
sync ready 2
pkill ${victim}
sync dead 2

[victim]
gm level 21
gm xp 5000
gm labor 100
tp 23039.76 11540.64 252.7
pump 3
sync ready 2
sync dead 2
gm revive ${victim}
pump 1
# CSStartSkill: skill 17063, Unit caster (self), Unit target (the priest), no skill object.
castraw 17063 502
# The effect sends the labor change first, then SCRecoverableExpPacket, then the exp delta.
expectpkt SCCharacterLaborPowerChangedPacket 12
expectpkt SCRecoverableExpPacket 5
expectpkt SCExpChangedPacket 5
